---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Veripharm Case | Austin Ban">
  <div class="gradient-block2" style="height: 100vh; text-align: center;">
    <div class="text-block mobile-app-header">
      <div class="small-12" data-aos="flip-up" data-aos-once="true" data-aos-duration="700">
        <h1 class="huge" style="text-align: center;">Veripharm — Distributed Health Hackathon Winner</h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="down-arrow bounce">
    <a href="#next"><i class="fa fa-arrow-down" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
  </div>

  <div id="next" class="index-block pink">
    <div class="text-block gradient-block2">
      <div class="small-12" data-aos="flip-up" data-aos-once="true" data-aos-duration="700">
        <h1>The planning phase.</h1>
        <p>After being made aware of the Distributed Health hackathon by a friend, I arrived armed only with my laptop. Though the hackathon was based on blockchain technology, I barely knew what blockchaining was. What we created in those 24 hours wound up winning 2 of the 5 prizes awarded, including the grand prize.</p>
        <p>Within a couple of hours, I found a team that needed an interface designer for their idea of creating a pharmaceutical tracking app using blockchaining. The team was composed of 2 software designers, a security guru, a long-time pharmaceutical employee, and myself.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="img-wrap">
    <img src="/images/veri-1.jpg" alt="Veripharm case image" class="case-image" loading="lazy" />
  </div>

  <div class="index-block">
    <div class="text-block">
      <div class="small-12" data-aos="flip-up" data-aos-once="true" data-aos-duration="700">
        <h1>Building the UI.</h1>
        <p>Because of our limited time frame, we decided to build the UI using Node.js. After the confusion of getting it set up, the rest was standard HTML and SASS development.</p>
        <h2>Veripharm was built using:</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><i class="fa fa-check" aria-hidden="true"></i> Node.js</li>
          <li><i class="fa fa-check" aria-hidden="true"></i> Tierion</li>
          <li><i class="fa fa-check" aria-hidden="true"></i> MongoDB</li>
          <li><i class="fa fa-check" aria-hidden="true"></i> Blockchain</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="img-wrap">
    <img src="/images/veri-2.jpg" alt="Veripharm case image" class="case-image" loading="lazy" />
  </div>

  <div class="index-block">
    <div class="text-block">
      <div class="small-12">
        <div data-aos="flip-up" data-aos-once="true" data-aos-duration="700">
          <h1>The take away.</h1>
          <p>When Veripharm was announced as the winning project, tears sprung into my eyes. The victory felt in that moment has carried me through many long nights buried in code.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="quote" data-aos="flip-up" data-aos-once="true" data-aos-duration="700">
          <h2>"Measure twice, cut once."</h2>
          <p>The principle of careful planning before execution was vital to finishing this project on time.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="quote" data-aos="flip-up" data-aos-once="true" data-aos-duration="700">
          <h2>"Do things that scare you."</h2>
          <p>Feelings of incompetency nearly kept me from even beginning this hackathon. What a mistake it would have been to limit myself because of my own fears.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="quote" data-aos="flip-up" data-aos-once="true" data-aos-duration="700">
          <h2>"Take care of yourself."</h2>
          <p>These 24 hours took 72 hours to recover from. Oh, and eat something other than pizza every now and then.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
